From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:30:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(miniwin): texture immediate-mode draws and
 decal-transparent meshes

A DirectDraw surface's IDirect3DTexture2 now has a handle, and
DrawIndexedPrimitive draws with stage 0's texture: the one SetTexture
set, or else the surface the TEXTUREHANDLE render state names. The draw
record carries it as an IDirect3DRMTexture, so a backend maps it with
GetTextureId as it does for retained-mode meshes.

The D3DRM device's FindPreferredTextureFormat answers 8-bit palettized
when asked for it, and RGB 565 otherwise. Texture::SetDecalTransparency
and SetDecalTransparentColor take effect.

The software backend's texture cache turns a surface colour key and a
decal colour into alpha-0 texels and remembers that they are a key. The
immediate rasterizer samples stage 0 perspective-correct, nearest or
bilinear by TEXTUREMAG, and applies stage 0's colour and alpha ops
(DISABLE, SELECTARG1/2, MODULATE, MODULATE2X/4X, ADD) to the texture and
the lit diffuse colour. With COLORKEYENABLE, key texels are not drawn and
do not bleed into filtered neighbours; without it they draw as their
colour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

